Falsifies `calendar::verification::unix_to_civil_and_back_is_the_identity`.

The defect: `Civil::from_unix` divides with truncating `/` where it needs `div_euclid`. Every instant of the
last day of 1969 that is not exactly midnight decodes to 1970-01-01, one day late.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(c.to_unix(), secs)` for a negative timestamp.

diff --git a/crates/calendar/src/lib.rs b/crates/calendar/src/lib.rs
index 332ce0020..1796e0c4d 100644
--- a/crates/calendar/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/calendar/src/lib.rs
@@ -384,3 +384,3 @@ impl Civil {
         // way a date library gets 1969-12-31 wrong.
-        let days = secs.div_euclid(SECONDS_PER_DAY);
+        let days = secs / SECONDS_PER_DAY;
         let sod = secs.rem_euclid(SECONDS_PER_DAY);
